      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The approach prioritizing pathways to citizenship and humanitarian processing is more likely to provide a long-term, stable solution for the country's economic and social needs. This is because a pathway to citizenship would allow undocumented immigrants to contribute to the economy, pay taxes, and access essential services, thereby reducing the burden on public resources. In contrast, increased border enforcement and tech-based security may only serve to deter more people from coming to the US, rather than addressing the root causes of migration and providing a solution for those already here.",
